  "docs_url": "https://documentation.unbounce.com/hc/en-us/articles/360001258266-Working-with-Users",
  "evidence": "Unbounce's user guide covers only inviting users by email and removing them by hand, its only SSO is personal \"Sign in with Google\" that admins cannot enforce, and a help-centre search for \"scim\" returns no articles.",
  "notes": "No SCIM and no SAML/OIDC SSO on any plan. Users are invited by email and given Viewer, Author or Administrator roles per client; removal is manual. Google SSO is a per-user \"Sign in with Google\" option that cannot be enforced, so it does not count as SSO. Pricing is flat per plan with user caps: Starter $22/mo and Build $74/mo (1 user each), Experiment $112/mo (3 users), Optimize $187/mo (5 users), all billed annually; Concierge (15 users) and Agency are Contact Sales. Experiment is the team plan as the first tier with more than one user. The public REST API can only read the current user or a user by id; it cannot create or remove users. Okta lists an Unbounce app (Single Sign-On use case only, last updated 2017). Status none by absence (rule 5).",
